35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really important stuff! It turns out a lot of people struggled to pay their renewals on time, and some even asked to pay in installments. We can't just assume everyone can pay a big lump sum!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are somewhat sobering. A small group of members accounts for the vast majority of attendance, while many others rarely appear. Some feel a certain unease about the cost relative to their limited participation.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, you're finally seeing it. I found that a tiny group is doing everything—including all the setup and locking up—while eighteen people didn't even show up once. It's a joke that they pay the same as the people carrying the club.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The financial data is equally stark. Seventy percent of our outgoings are fixed costs—hall hire, insurance, and storage—which must be paid regardless of attendance. We cannot simply ignore these baseline expenses in our calculations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I found something really important! A lot of people who came to our taster evenings didn't join because they didn't want to pay for a whole year at once. Even the mid-year joiners needed special calculations!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, that's exactly what I saw in the bank statements! It's a bit scary that so many people struggled with the lump sum. If we keep it that way, we might be losing great new members before they even start!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It is concerning that our members feel a sense of hesitation. When the cost of belonging becomes a source of unease, it creates a barrier that prevents people from simply coming home to the club.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, stop talking about ""barriers"" and ""homes."" The real barrier is that the people actually running this place are being taken advantage of. Why should the nine people doing all the work subsidize eighteen ghosts?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, while your frustration is understandable, we must consider the cost of management. I found that chasing individual payments takes six times more effort than a yearly collection. A complex, tiered system may increase the treasurer's burden to an unsustainable level.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I get that it's a lot of work, but if we make it too hard for people to join, we won't have any members left to manage! We have to find a way to make it easy for everyone.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I understand the treasurer's struggle, but we can't just ignore the fact that people are struggling to pay! If we keep guessing and picking a number that's too high or too rigid, we're just asking for more trouble.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Perhaps we can find a middle path. If we create a structure that reduces the psychological weight of the fee, we might encourage those who hesitate to return to us more frequently. Peace of mind is invaluable.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, peace of mind doesn't pay the hall hire or reward the people actually doing the work. We can't just be ""gentle"" while the core members are getting burned out. We need a system that reflects actual contribution.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, reflecting actual contribution sounds fair in theory, but it is a logistical nightmare. If we implement a pay-as-you-go or tiered system, we are essentially sentencing the next treasurer to endless hours of chasing small sums.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I don't want anyone to feel burned out! But if we make the fees too complicated or based on who shows up, it might feel like we're judging people. Let's keep it simple and welcoming!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, I agree that we should keep it welcoming! But @Toshio, we can't just stick to a lump sum if people can't afford it. We need a plan that's realistic about our money and our members' wallets!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we are all touching upon different facets of the same tension. Whether it is financial strain, administrative burden, or the feeling of unfairness, the result is a lack of harmony. We must find a balance that restores a sense of ease.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, harmony is just a word for ignoring the problem. We have a core group of nine people doing everything and eighteen people who don't even exist here. That's not a lack of harmony; it's a lack of fairness. We need a real solution.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, fairness is not just about who attends, but also about who manages the system. If we create a complex structure to punish the ""ghosts,"" we simply shift the burden onto the treasurer. We must prioritize a sustainable administrative process.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, @Takumi, I hear you both! But if we start tracking every single person's attendance just for the fees, it'll feel like we're watching them. Let's find a way to be fair without making everyone feel like they're being monitored!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
