60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at the options, Option A is what we did before, and we know people struggled with that lump sum! If we just guess a number again, we're going to have the same problems with late payments.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A may be simple, but it seems to be the source of the hesitation I discovered. If the cost feels like a burden, members will continue to weigh their decision to attend rather than simply coming.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is a joke. It's exactly what's causing the problem—the people who do everything are subsidizing the ghosts. We can't just go back to a system that rewards people for not showing up.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option C is a logistical disaster. Based on the treasurer's logs, chasing individual payments is six times more labor-intensive than a yearly collection. We cannot commit the next treasurer to that level of burnout.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I totally agree that we shouldn't make the treasurer's life a nightmare! But Option A is what scared away those taster guests. Maybe Option B is a good middle ground? It's simpler than C!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, I think you're on to something! Option B lets people choose what they can afford and what they actually want, so it's not just one scary lump sum for everyone. It feels way more realistic!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Option B offers a gentle compromise. By allowing members to select a level that matches their own comfort and capacity, we remove the psychological barrier that makes them hesitate to join us. It restores a sense of peace.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, ""comfort"" isn't the issue here. Option B is only a win if the tiers actually reflect the work being done. If the ""ghosts"" can just pick a cheap tier and still coast, it doesn't fix the unfairness.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, the issue is that any system attempting to ""fix"" unfairness by tracking participation increases the administrative load. Option B is more sustainable than C, but we must ensure the tiers are fixed and not subject to constant adjustment.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get that, but if we make it too strict, it'll feel like we're judging people! Option B lets everyone find their own place without us having to watch their every move. It keeps things friendly!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, as long as the tiers are set at the start, it shouldn't be too much extra work! It's way better than guessing a single number and hoping for the best. I want us to have a budget we can actually count on!","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe Option B is the most compassionate choice. It acknowledges that not everyone interacts with the club in the same way, allowing those who feel uneasy to return without the weight of an oversized fee.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, compassion doesn't fix the fact that nine people are doing all the work. But if Option B means the people who actually use the club pay for the value they get, it's better than A. I'm tired of the ghosts getting a free ride.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mio, while you see it as a small addition, any deviation from a single flat fee increases the risk of errors and chasing. However, compared to the chaos of Option C, Option B is the only viable alternative to A. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":45,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm with you, @Toshio! Option B is way better than C, and it's more welcoming than A. It lets new friends join in without feeling overwhelmed, and we don't have to monitor everyone. I vote for Option B!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm so glad we're all seeing the benefits of Option B! It solves the lump sum problem, keeps the treasurer sane, and is fairer than just guessing. I'm voting for Option B too!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"It is a relief to see us in such harmony. Option B removes the hesitation that weighs on our members' hearts, allowing them to return to us with a peaceful mind. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not happy about the ghosts, but Option B is the only way to stop the blatant unfairness of Option A without killing the treasurer. It's a start. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is clear. Option B balances the need for financial accessibility and fairness without imposing the unsustainable administrative burden of Option C. It is the most rational choice for the club's stability. I vote for Option B.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,Yay! I'm so happy we all agree! Option B keeps things friendly for the new people and doesn't make us act like police. Let's make next year the best one yet! I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
